{
  "itemid": "1169911",
  "languages": {
    "english": {
      "app[content][about]": "[p]Data Breach Inc. is an arcade incremental about breaking into hostile corporate infrastructure one risky sortie at a time. Pilot a breach rig, mine the firewall for resources, crack daemon cores, extract before the run turns ugly, and use the payout to make the next breach go deeper.[/p][p]Every flight is part action run, part upgrade puzzle. You choose how hard to push: carve a safe route, chase valuable blocks, pressure a daemon core, or turn back early and bank the haul. Money, XP, and root kernels feed permanent upgrades for damage, attack speed, cargo, fuel, drones, range, payout scaling, and core-cracking power.[/p][p]The firewall does not sit still. Deeper layers hit harder, daemon cores fight back, and defensive pressure forces cleaner routes instead of mindless grinding. Learn the layout, tune your rig, and turn messy extraction runs into faster clears.[/p][p]The demo is built around defeating the demo breach and chasing a cleaner time on the Defeat Demo leaderboard. The full Data Breach Inc. structure also connects side operations into the campaign, including Red Sky Defense and Deepcore, with resources and unlocks feeding back into the central breach.[/p][p]Features:[/p][p]- Arcade breach sorties built around mining, movement, survival, and extraction[/p][p]- Persistent firewall progress across runs[/p][p]- Permanent upgrades for damage, speed, cargo, fuel, drones, range, payouts, and core damage[/p][p]- Daemon core encounters with escalating defensive pressure[/p][p]- Multiple resource paths: cash, XP, and root kernels[/p][p]- Demo clear target with leaderboard-ready timing[/p][p]- Connected side operations in the full Data Breach Inc. structure[/p][p]- Short runs with long-term incremental progression[/p]",
      "app[content][short_description]": "Pilot a breach rig into hostile corporate infrastructure. Mine the firewall, crack daemon cores, extract your haul, and buy permanent upgrades between sorties.",
      "app[content][sysreqs][windows][min][osversion]": "Windows 7+",
      "app[content][sysreqs][windows][min][processor]": "2 Ghz",
      "app[content][sysreqs][windows][min][graphics]": "128MB, OpenGL 3+"
